actually, i don't think the current game does justice to gender.  i'm
not saying i'm completely unhappy but there must be much more that the
game could do to enforce gender distinctions.  under such a scheme there
would be real incentive to choose to be male or female since this would
involve alternative strategies.  currently there are only cosmetic
differences and that in part is why the game is allowed to get away
with random gender changes.

i don't think i'm a bigot, my problem is that my identity (or alter-ego)
is male and the game has arbitrarily decided to make me a female in
order to hilite some clever cosmetic distinctions.  i would actually
choose to be female once in awhile (in nethack) if there were real
differences in making the choice.  i think the problem is on par with
cats not being dogs.  because of the symmetrical nature of my argument
i don't think i'm a bigot but ...

perhaps i am a {sexual} bigot and can't see it. no harm intended!
